\DOC X86_ADD_RETURN_STACK_TAC

\TYPE {X86_ADD_RETURN_STACK_TAC : thm * (thm option array) -> thm -> term -> int -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Discharges a universally quantified {ensures} specification for a stack-using
x86 subroutine from a corresponding core-function specification, either closing
the goal or reducing it to a single residual trace-equality obligation with the
symbolic post-return state available as assumptions.

\DESCRIBE
The arguments are {execth : thm * (thm option array)}, the machine-code
execution package for the program concerned (a code-length theorem paired with
per-instruction decoding data); {coreth : thm}, the already-proved
specification of the core routine from which the goal's specification is to be
derived; {reglist : term}, a term that is a list of registers, naming the
callee-saved registers whose save/restore is to be accounted for; and
{stackoff : int}, the integer size of the stack frame reserved below the
incoming stack pointer. It applies to an assumption-free goal whose conclusion
is {forall x1 ... xn. A ==> ensures ...}, possibly wrapped in an outer
existential over an event function, and either solves it outright, leaving no
subgoals, or leaves exactly one subgoal. In the latter case the quantified
variables are fixed, the hypotheses {A} of the specification are broken apart
and placed in the assumption list in expanded form {A'} (overlap conditions
rewritten to their {nonoverlapping_modulo} form), accompanied by a large set of
further assumptions {st} recording the symbolically computed state after return
— register, flag and stack-memory contents, the loaded code, the accumulated
{MAYCHANGE} relation between the initial and final states, and the final event
list — and the conclusion {u} is what remains of the postcondition, typically
an existential equation about the event trace.
{
           ?- forall x1 ... xn. A ==> t
      ==================================== X86_ADD_RETURN_STACK_TAC execth coreth reglist stackoff
           (no subgoals)   or   A', st ?- u
}

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces, the goals have this specification shape with no prior
assumptions, and only these two outcomes occur.

\ENDDOC
